# Webpieces tooling working dir: ai-hook-rules bootstrap/cache, instruct-ai docs,
# and per-feature git workflow dirs (merge-/review-/pr-, 30-day retention)
.webpieces/

# Claude Code subagent worktrees — linked git worktrees, never committed.
#
# NOT `.claude/`: .claude/agents/** and .claude/review/** are TRACKED and define the
# REQUIRED PR reviewers (backwards-compat-reviewer). Ignoring the whole directory would
# drop the review gate out of the repo on the next clone, and the failure would look like
# "the reviewer stopped being required" — which nobody notices quickly.
#
# This entry is load-bearing, not hygiene: nx honours .gitignore when it scans the
# workspace, so without it nx walks into every worktree and finds a second and third copy
# of all 27 project.json files. EVERY nx command on the primary clone then dies instantly
# with MultipleProjectsWithSameNameError for as long as any agent worktree exists.
.claude/worktrees/

# Stray review.json at the REPO ROOT. The real one lives in .webpieces/pr-review/<branch>/review.json
# (gitignored with the rest of .webpieces/). A root-level copy is always an accident: it is what lands
# when an isolated agent cannot Write to the shared checkout and `cp`s its verdict to the wrong place.
# Committed once by #647 that way. Ignored so the next one never reaches a PR.
/review.json
